69,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, the ticketing fees are high. Replacing them saves money long-term.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,May,,"I support A. The pilot proved it works, and it fixes the fee issue.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I oppose D. We cannot staff it. I lean towards A for stability.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,I prefer B. It targets the actual delay in the mid-city.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I am wary of C, but the lift capacity is a strong point.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I vote for A. It resolves the financial leak in the ticketing fees.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
